# Project-specific
*.mp4
*.avi
*.mov
*.mkv

# Scrape output - regenerable, keep it out of history. The export is TSV now, so
# an extension rule cannot carry this on its own: a correction ledger is TSV too,
# and those are the one thing under a site that is meant to be kept. Ignore the
# site data directories by path instead, and leave ledger/ and history/ tracked.
*.csv
/sites/*/data/*

# Each directory under sites/ is one source site: its profile, its correction
# ledger, its scraped data, and the working notes taken from it — all of which
# name the real people the site is about. Each is a separate private repository,
# cloned into place; git does not recurse into an ignored path, so nothing about
# them, not even their existence, reaches this repository.
#
# Ignore the contents rather than the directory, so the README explaining what
# belongs there can still be tracked. Anchored to the root, so an unrelated
# sites/ elsewhere in the tree is unaffected.
# /sites/*
!/sites/README.md

# config/ holds credentials that are not tied to any one site — the OAuth client
# secret for uploading. data/ is scrape output. Ignore both wholesale rather than
# by extension: the rule has to hold for the next file type someone reaches for,
# not just the ones used so far. The publishable example profiles live in
# src/video_migrator/profiles/ instead.
config/*
data/*
